				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doodslayer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7105251); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7105251&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607715300" alt="DoodSlayer" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7105251)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doodslayer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7105251); return false;" >DoodSlayer</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607711622 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Dec 2020 18:33</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13909371/the-censor-robot">The Censor Robot.</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842467">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: -J SCP.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: A small, square cube with a monitor screen with a robot face that randomly [REDACTED] any text written about it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> At first, it seems like this little guy's just a robot. It's sentient, but it has the intelligence of a cat, and otherwise can't do much, seeing how it's just a cube with a face. However, anyone who actually tries to write about it would have random words or sentences be replaced by [[REDACTED]]. For example, &quot;During testing, the subject showed [[REDACTED]] in the box placed in front of it&quot;. It doesn't have any control over this ability, nor shows awareness of it in the first place. The article is basically about its poor researcher, as he tries to make a comprehensive article out of it without it [[REDACTED]] every word.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/ Attention Grabber</strong>: I'm aware that there are a few SCPs that censor their own articles. However, the [[REDACTED]] here is completely random, and in fact never seems to cover up anything really important, only really being inconvenient at worst.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Yes, this is kinda satire of the overuse of [[REDACTED]], if you're wondering.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

